the relationship between the quarian and  the geth is one of the main through  lines of the mass effect series  an analog for the broader theme of ai  servitude and  sapience by the time the events of the  first mass effect take place  the quarian are a downbeat nomadic  people living aboard a flotilla of ships  and the geth threatened to wipe out life  in the galaxy  on this week's episode of mass effect  lore let's start with the quarian or as  they're known to the geth  the creators and how they ended up  fighting for survival  against the very things they created for  more videos like this one and coverage  of the upcoming mass effect legendary  edition  make sure to like this video and  subscribe  the quarian home planet of ranoc is an  arid desert in the milky way  due to its dry nature and lack of  insects growing and cultivating food was  difficult but the whole planet wasn't  completely barren the southern continent  had  excellent farmland the quarian are a  technologically advanced race and used  their knowledge to create the geth  a subservient labor force designed to  help in fact  geth translates to servant of the people  in the quarian language of kellish  the citadel council had strict rules  prohibiting the creation of artificial  intelligence  so the geth were initially designed as a  virtual intelligence  but the quarian discovered that the get  they'd made weren't all that clever  over time they tinkered with the geth  and began to network them together  which enabled them to do more and more  complex tasks  while geth can't share sensory  information they can communicate with  each other at the speed of light  and share their processing power  shifting it to where it's needed  with a collective conscious of sorts  over time they began to gain  intelligence at a rapid rate  and were eventually capable of logic and  reason  the geth had evolved  one day a geth asked its overseer an  innocent but profound  question does this unit have a soul  terrified at the implications of the  question and perhaps the answer to it  the quarians ordered immediate  termination of the geth  not just the unit who asked the question  all of them but it was too late  in the beginning only some geth  retaliated merely to defend those units  who were unable to fight for themselves  but the quarians doggedly chased them  down even going so far as to declare  martial law  as well as imprison and kill their own  who were hiding death  by 1895 the two races were engaged in  all-out war  known throughout the galaxy as the geth  war but to the geth as  the morning war because of the shared  network geth don't really die  instead when one is terminated its  program is merely transmitted elsewhere  as a result the geth were victorious  within a year killing over 99  of the pre-walk warian population the  quarian who were left  fled the planet taking to space aboard  their ships  while the geth didn't follow the  quarians to space their troubles did  believing that the citadel council would  grant them aid the quarians pleaded for  help  only to be cast out and have their  embassy aboard the citadel closed  the reaction from the council seemed  over the top but the quarians had broken  one of the council's strictest laws  don't interfere with or create  artificial intelligence  their doom was of their own making and  now they were left to reckon with it on  their own  in the deep dark depths of space  life aboard the flotilla or migrant  fleet is far from easy  with no homeland or council help  resources are extremely scarce and the  quarians had to adapt to ensure the  survival of their species  the quarians have a weakened immune  system caused by their harsh homeland  and then  exacerbated by years spent aboard  sterile spaceships  so they each wear a special suit to  shield them from the outside world  their envirosuit the suit protects them  from infections that might otherwise  kill them  and if it gets ripped its automatic seal  compensates to mitigate the spread of  infection  despite receiving vaccinations against  various diseases throughout their lives  quarians are typically unwilling to  remove their suits  and if they do must undertake extreme  precautions first  which makes having relations difficult  in fact linking envirosuits with another  is one of the most  intimate things a quarian can do as it  carries huge risks even in sterile  environments  but it's not like the quarians are  getting down with it all the time either  there's actually a law prohibiting  having more than one child  unless the population is in decline  quarian society is built upon securing  the continuation of their species  they work together as a community more  frequently than other mass effect races  with young quarians undertaking a  pilgrimage when they come of age  in order to expand their horizons but  also to prove their worth to the fleet  by bringing back something useful  like technology information or resources  in order to prevent inbreeding upon  their return from their pilgrimage  newly anointed adult quarians choose a  brand new ship in the flotilla to live  and settle down on  presenting their new captain with  whatever they picked up on their travels  the quarians don't use credits the  regular currency used throughout the  galaxy  instead valuing food medicine and  technology  they keep a close eye on food and  medicine to ensure that there's enough  to go around  but they are freer with personal items  with limited space aboard the flotilla  and a lack of attachment to  things the quarian donate what they  don't want or need and others take it to  use  so nothing goes to waste the quarians  have a civilian government called the  conclave that makes the majority of  decisions for the fleet  and there is an admiralty board that  oversees them in the most serious  situations the admiralty board can  overturn a government decision  but once they've done so they must  either all quit their posts  or face being arrested as the fleet is  still technically under martial law from  the geth war  most issues never even make it to the  conclave and are handled by the ship's  captain  instead due to a lack of space aboard  the flotilla's ships  the worst criminals in society are  exiled because why waste resources on  those who aren't contributing  but that's just one of the many reasons  the rest of the galaxy is untrusting of  the quarians after creating the geth  exiling their worst prisoners as well as  their habit of moving through systems to  scavenge and mine whatever they can  they're often seen as second-class  citizens and thieves  but the quarians didn't want to be a  burden on the rest of their galaxy they  dreamt of retaking their homeworlds  but the quarian homeworlds weren't  exactly fully populated by the geth  after their rebellion  instead of building a civilization upon  ranuk the geth chose to live in computer  hubs aboard spaceships  monitoring the extranet for any  information they could use and opening  fire upon any ships that came near them  while the geth kept tabs on the rest of  the galaxy they preferred to advance  their own race alone away from any  interference  they did however keep brown up clean of  debris out of respect  and as a memorial to the creators that  were killed there they spent their time  working on creating a mainframe that  could house the programs of every single  geth unit  a goal that they'd been working towards  for a couple of hundred years  however the reaper sovereign approached  the geth and offered them  advanced technology that they could use  in turn for their assistance  only a few took up sovereign's offer to  serve and were then called heretics by  the remaining geth  who wanted to create their project with  their own technology  and were suspicious of the reapers  calling them the old machines  the reapers despite obtaining a new  workforce were repulsed by the devotion  shown by the geth  who praised the reapers as being the  pinnacle of a.i evolution  these geth left the main geth network  and followed sovereign and his  right-hand man  sarin across the galaxy which is where  we meet them at the start of the first  mass effect game  if you're picking up mass effect for the  first time with the legendary edition or  you're just revisiting it after a few  years away  hopefully this video has helped you  understand the quarian geth conflict  better  we've got more lore videos up on the  channel right now including ones on the  krogan and the genophage  as well as the protheans and for more  mass effect make sure to subscribe  we'll catch you next time  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

